.TH SIAD 4
.SH NAME
siad \- the assistant server (port "sia")
.SH SYNOPSIS
Port
.BR sia .
.B /bin/siad
is started on demand by
.BR init (8),
stopped after 15 minutes unused; it may use 4.5 GiB at most.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B siad
answers questions with a language model: the local one (SIEOS's own engine
on this machine's processors, a GGUF file) or a remote one with an
OpenAI-compatible API, as
.BR sia.conf (5)
says.
.PP
A client opens a session, sends a message, and receives the answer in
pieces: the reply to SIA_ASK comes at once, then each SIA_NEXT returns the
next piece.
Several sessions may run at once, each with its own conversation; they take
turns, one piece each.
Every conversation is saved as it goes, in /var/sia/UID (the caller's uid,
as the kernel stamped it), so it can be resumed after a restart; a long one
is compacted (its older turns replaced by a summary the model writes).
sia also keeps a few facts about each user, given to the model at the start
of every conversation.
.SH MESSAGES
.TP
.B SIA_OPEN
w[1] = flags (SIA_RESUME: w[2] = a conversation, 0: the last) \-> a
session; reply w[1] = the conversation, w[2] = 1 if resumed.
.TP
.B SIA_ASK
w[1] = session; sbuf = the user's message (UTF-8, at most 4096 bytes) \-> 0.
.TP
.B SIA_NEXT
w[1] = session; rbuf <\- the next piece \-> bytes, 0: the end.
.TP
.BR SIA_STOP ", " SIA_CLOSE
stop generating now; forget the session.
.TP
.B SIA_INFO
rbuf <\- sia_info_t: the backend, ready, sessions, context length, memory
used, the last speed (tokens/s x 100), the model's name.
.TP
.B SIA_CONFIG
(root) sbuf = "key=value": saved in /etc/sia.conf (the API key in
/etc/sia.key); siad then ends and init starts it again with it.
.TP
.BR SIA_LIST ", " SIA_FORGET
the caller's conversations, "id<TAB>turns<TAB>tokens<TAB>title" lines,
newest first; delete one (0: all).
.TP
.B SIA_FACTS
w[1] = SIA_F_GET, SIA_F_ADD (sbuf), SIA_F_DEL (w[2] = its line), SIA_F_CLEAR,
SIA_F_OFFERED (facts the model proposed, to be confirmed).
.TP
.B SIA_CONTEXT
w[1] = session; sbuf = extra instructions for this conversation.
.SH FILES
.TP
.BR /etc/sia.conf ", " /etc/sia.key
settings; the API key (root only)
.TP
.B /models/*.gguf
local models
.TP
.B /var/sia/UID
each user's conversations and facts (siad alone)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sia (1),
.BR sia.conf (5),
.BR atlas (4)
